WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(applause)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.440
- All right

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.001
This is like a fella show, I like it.

00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:07.630
Well, congratulations on the film.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:08.510
I was telling y'all backstage

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.040
you have to be just like freaking out.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.150
This is a really great film
that y'all are part of.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.450
You all did a really,
really fantastic job.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.780
Have any of y'all played basketball,

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:17.613
you want to tell everybody?

00:00:17.613 --> 00:00:18.530
You're in a basketball movie,

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.721
so I'm gonna lead with that.

00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:21.260
(laugh)

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.093
- You haven't.

00:00:22.093 --> 00:00:23.885
- No, I've never picked up a basketball.

00:00:23.885 --> 00:00:25.510
(laugh)

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:27.620
I'm a football guy.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.453
Yeah, I've always--

00:00:28.453 --> 00:00:29.286
- It shows.

00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:30.667
- It definitely shows.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.640
- So, do y'all just like lie?

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.950
When the audition comes up, you're like,

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.070
yeah, I play all the time.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:37.390
- My manager lied for me.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.950
She told production
that I scored 17 points,

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.680
10 assists, six rebounds.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.007
And they thought it was great
until they saw me in person.

00:00:46.007 --> 00:00:48.290
(laugh)

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.880
- Melvin, did you ever play?

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.410
- I played a basketballer
on television a few times.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.810
I went from playing like
the best basketball player

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:55.970
in a country or high school,

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.870
best basketball player in the NBA,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.934
and I got to play Marcus was
the worst player on the team.

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:02.680
(laugh)

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:03.722
- So, what about you Will?

00:01:03.722 --> 00:01:07.610
- I grew up playing baseball
and then I slowly like

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.400
realized that I wasn't
that great at baseball

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.350
and then I wasn't gonna
do anything with it

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.790
and kind of became a
feeder band nerd instead

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.490
and did like trombone and theater.

00:01:17.657 --> 00:01:20.300
But I, you know, for this movie,
I worked on my shot a lot.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.410
So, I hope it paid off.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.980
- I know, I'm like all
those three pointers.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:24.820
- We don't know if it went in.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.500
They cut, they freeze frame right before.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.370
- Lot of CGI.

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:30.620
- Make me look good,
Brandon how 'bout you?

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.480
- Oh, yeah, I've been playing
basketball my whole life.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.750
I've been playing all sports.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.283
I was terrible as a child,

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.870
and then I like kind of
picks it up a little bit more

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:41.400
and I had a little
foundation to bring to this.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.880
- They they had a really
challenging thing,

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.560
which was the audition
was not just the acting,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.580
but they also auditioned,
playing basketball.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.800
So the finalists as actors
were all playing basketball

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.187
against each other.

00:01:52.187 --> 00:01:53.950
I mean, I really felt for him, you know,

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.570
and then be like, okay,
you guys can go home.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:56.540
Okay, next, you know.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.168
And I was like, man, this is brutal.

00:01:58.168 --> 00:02:00.317
- I am sweating in my
pants right now for you.

00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:01.150
(laughs)

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:03.180
I would be like, ya know what, we lied.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.680
I'm not really great.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:05.740
Did you play sports?

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:06.573
Did you play basketball?

00:02:06.573 --> 00:02:07.510
- I did not play basketball.

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:11.430
No, I didn't, I don't
claim to play basketball.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.207
I never told anybody I
didn't play basketball.

00:02:13.207 --> 00:02:14.350
You got me?

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.343
- I actually told them
I suck at basketball.

00:02:16.343 --> 00:02:17.305
- Yeah, I was not good.
(laugh)

00:02:17.305 --> 00:02:18.645
- And that was actually
and the director was like,

00:02:18.645 --> 00:02:19.478
he was really funny, he said,

00:02:19.478 --> 00:02:21.350
"That's what I'm most worried about."

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:22.330
You don't know The game.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.120
I was like, I don't really know the game.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.050
And so he was like, the acting,
this stuff, all the drama.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:28.280
He was like, you gotta.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.050
So I watched a lot of
tape of coaches and stuff.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.030
And the thing that was
most important to me was

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.820
to develop a relationship with these guys.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.550
Develop a kind of a rapport.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.410
And I think we did, we had a good time.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.632
- It's great, the chemistry is great.

00:02:40.632 --> 00:02:41.465
I don't know.

00:02:41.465 --> 00:02:42.298
I mean, you're all great actors

00:02:42.298 --> 00:02:44.160
if it wasn't really great in person.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.810
But I know that it's awkward
to ask in front of them,

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:47.830
but I want the T.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:51.520
What is the best story,
the best Ben story?

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.315
Will, do you have one?

00:02:53.315 --> 00:02:54.148
- You want me to start?

00:02:54.148 --> 00:02:55.550
- Yes, I do, I'm putting you on the spot.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:56.383
Don't be afraid.

00:02:56.383 --> 00:02:57.360
- Well, Okay.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.282
- Be afraid.

00:02:58.282 --> 00:02:59.115
(laugh)

00:02:59.115 --> 00:02:59.948
- [Kelly] I will defend you.

00:02:59.948 --> 00:03:00.930
I will hold Batman back.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.840
- Okay, well, when we were shooting,

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.370
there's a scene in the movie
I don't give away a lot.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.758
But a skirmish breaks out and we,

00:03:07.758 --> 00:03:09.690
you know, the benches cleared.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.360
And I remember I'm in like
the group of all these dudes

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.450
and we're fighting and whatever.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:15.550
Fake fighting.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.710
And I just feel this
dude come up behind me

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.280
and just like grab me like this

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.390
and just rip me out of the pile.

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.150
And then I look back
and it was Ben Affleck

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:26.507
and I was like, that's how
strong Batman is supposed to be.

00:03:26.507 --> 00:03:27.953
(all laugh)
(applause)

00:03:27.953 --> 00:03:29.203
It makes sense.

00:03:31.874 --> 00:03:34.350
I feel bad for the Joker's like henchmen.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.253
Like, he's legit.

00:03:36.217 --> 00:03:38.440
- Do you think Batman would
have picked the smallest guy?

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.401
To pull out of there?

00:03:39.401 --> 00:03:40.234
(laugh)

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:41.846
- He would have picked you, yeah.

00:03:41.846 --> 00:03:43.531
- If I was really strong I
would have been like, Melvin!

00:03:43.531 --> 00:03:45.660
(laughing)

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.363
- Did anybody else get
a bear hug from Batman?

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:52.580
- No, but wow, man.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.180
We were three weeks in shooting
I didn't have no lines,

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.010
We were just doing all
of the basketball stuff.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.450
So when we had the scene

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:02.090
where he introduces himself
as the coach, I was so happy.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.694
I'm like, I finally get to speak finally.

00:04:03.694 --> 00:04:04.527
Finally!

00:04:04.527 --> 00:04:08.540
And so I remember when I
got ready to say my lines,

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.330
and this guy cuts my line off.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:14.490
And so it was, I let it slide.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.880
I gave him so slack.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:16.960
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.433
(laughter and applause)

00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:22.300
- I'll let Ben Affleck slide.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.795
- Left the heater in the back, you know?

00:04:23.795 --> 00:04:24.870
- You are so bold!

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.572
- No, he didn't let anything slide.

00:04:26.572 --> 00:04:27.405
Tell the story.

00:04:27.405 --> 00:04:29.310
- No, I didn't 'cause
he did it want more time

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.387
and I was like, oh no.

00:04:30.387 --> 00:04:32.780
I'm not taking this.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:33.613
Ben Affleck who?

00:04:33.613 --> 00:04:36.090
(laugh)

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.990
So I just remember,

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:39.580
I was talking with Melvin in the group.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.023
I said, I'm about to tell Ben Affleck off.

00:04:43.676 --> 00:04:44.509
- [Kelly] Get off my Line.

00:04:44.509 --> 00:04:46.440
- And they were like, you
know, you crazy, don't do it.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.940
And then I ran over and I sprinted,

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.620
and I hit it right on the
chest was like, "Hey?"

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.522
I was like, "Hey, man,
you stepping on my lines?

00:04:52.522 --> 00:04:53.355
What's up with that?"

00:04:53.355 --> 00:04:54.540
You know what I mean?

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.373
- [Kelly] I'm proud of my line.

00:04:55.373 --> 00:04:56.206
I been waiting a minute to say it.

00:04:56.206 --> 00:04:58.130
- I told him, Ben Affleck,
you're Ben Affleck?

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:58.990
You win this movie.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:04:59.823
You got all the lines.

00:04:59.823 --> 00:05:00.866
I don't got that many lines.

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:01.754
You know what I mean?

00:05:01.754 --> 00:05:02.587
(laugh)

00:05:02.587 --> 00:05:04.340
I need all the chances I can get

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.310
and I had the script,

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.510
and I was telling him that oh my God.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:09.656
- This story has grown.

00:05:09.656 --> 00:05:10.610
I mean.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.443
- I punched him in the chest.

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:14.450
- The truth is I stepped on his line once.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.478
His line was what?

00:05:15.478 --> 00:05:17.478
(laugh)

00:05:18.345 --> 00:05:19.762
I looked past it.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.090
I didn't even think about it.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:23.110
And then he gave the,

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:23.960
hey man, hey man.

00:05:25.335 --> 00:05:27.490
Yeah, what's going on?

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.323
That's my line.

00:05:28.323 --> 00:05:29.479
You stepped on my line.

00:05:29.479 --> 00:05:30.734
- Don't make me sound like that.

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:32.128
- And now he's like, yo huh?

00:05:32.128 --> 00:05:32.961
My line!

00:05:34.207 --> 00:05:36.088
And I did look at the other
guys and they were like,

00:05:36.088 --> 00:05:36.921
(groans)

00:05:36.921 --> 00:05:37.754
- He looking at me.

00:05:37.754 --> 00:05:39.530
It was the same clip that
they show before we came out.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:40.710
- Yeah, they're spitting facts.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:41.950
He cut that off.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:43.350
- I was like, I did respect it.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:47.590
I was like, this guy is not
gonna let any take his line.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:48.443
My line is what!

00:05:49.335 --> 00:05:51.034
I'm gonna say my line!

00:05:51.034 --> 00:05:52.470
- That's my favorite.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:53.950
That's so rogue.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:57.290
And I love how your
story turned into that.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.253
And he was like, now the line was what.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:00.923
- Right?

00:06:00.923 --> 00:06:02.310
I'm acting like I got some big monologue.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:04.110
- I just, ya know, sweep the leg.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:05.267
(laughing)

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:06.628
- It's amaze.

00:06:06.628 --> 00:06:07.461
(claps)

00:06:07.461 --> 00:06:11.220
- All right, I ask everyone
to bring one hashtag

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:13.200
throwback Thursday photo
with a story behind it.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.690
I will go first because mine is probably

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:16.690
the most embarrassing.

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:17.523
Where's it at?

00:06:17.523 --> 00:06:20.700
Okay, so my mom, we were real broke.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:23.060
Because my mom's a teacher
and they make no money.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.490
It's horrible.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:28.180
Anyway so my mom would do this thing

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.453
where we couldn't afford
to go on vacations.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:33.870
She just cut our pictures
out around our head

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.817
and then place us on landscapes.

00:06:35.817 --> 00:06:36.650
- Oh wow.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:39.216
- So this was my favorite
trip to the Swiss Alps

00:06:39.216 --> 00:06:40.049
(laugh)

00:06:40.049 --> 00:06:42.370
This is my favorite.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:43.633
Yeah.

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.290
Like she would just take my random photos.

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:48.300
And here's the best part,

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.560
we didn't probably pay for that either.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.150
The you know they give you like the one

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.790
that says like photo on it

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:54.920
like and you just kind of, what,

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.240
would chop the bottom off.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.270
And then you don't have
to pay for the pictures.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:06:59.103
Note to self.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.680
But anyway, this was my throwback.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.420
My mom was, well, she was artistic.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:05.550
You beautiful woman you.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:06.383
Brandon.

00:07:06.383 --> 00:07:07.216
We're gonna go Brandon first.

00:07:07.216 --> 00:07:08.880
Here's Brandon's throwback.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:12.360
Oh my gosh, you're so cute.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:13.360
You are so cute.

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:15.092
Is that fake behind you or real?

00:07:15.092 --> 00:07:17.092
(laugh)

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:19.622
- You talking about the
Jheri curl behind my head?

00:07:19.622 --> 00:07:20.455
- [Kelly] No.

00:07:20.455 --> 00:07:21.288
- That's all real.

00:07:21.288 --> 00:07:22.121
(laughing)

00:07:22.121 --> 00:07:22.954
- [Kelly] No, the scene.

00:07:22.954 --> 00:07:24.110
- No, that's fake people in the back.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.520
- [Kelly] I know, I was just kidding.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:26.373
My landscape was cooler.

00:07:26.373 --> 00:07:28.610
- [Ben] You guys both have fake pictures.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:30.960
- People are really into the fake thing.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.110
All right, Will is next?

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:33.517
Let's see it.

00:07:33.517 --> 00:07:35.184
Oh come on, so cute.

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.360
Oh you need to be in a superhero movie.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.804
- I was everyone except
Batman, unfortunately.

00:07:41.804 --> 00:07:42.777
(laugh)

00:07:42.777 --> 00:07:44.456
- Yeah, but that's basically last year.

00:07:44.456 --> 00:07:46.456
(laugh)

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:48.530
- What's going on here though?

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.730
Are you flying off the tree or what?

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:53.760
- I don't know, I hope
onto a ladder or something.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.430
And I don't think that
was very high up though.

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:56.263
So we're good.

00:07:56.263 --> 00:07:57.110
- All right here.

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:57.943
Melvin!

00:07:58.785 --> 00:08:00.750
Melvin, you cutie.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.583
- [Ben] Lakers.

00:08:01.583 --> 00:08:02.416
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:08:02.416 --> 00:08:03.910
- Yeah, yeah, die hard Lakers fan.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:04.782
Yep.

00:08:04.782 --> 00:08:06.616
(applause)

00:08:06.616 --> 00:08:08.196
- All right, Charles is next.

00:08:08.196 --> 00:08:09.749
Let's see Charles'.

00:08:09.749 --> 00:08:10.830
(laughter)

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.330
- [Ben] Oh my God!

00:08:13.866 --> 00:08:17.130
- Oh my gosh, you little player.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:17.970
What are you wearing a suit?

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:20.470
Are you in like a show?

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:21.757
- No, so growing up as a--

00:08:21.757 --> 00:08:23.577
- Was is that, prohibition night?

00:08:23.577 --> 00:08:25.827
(laughter)

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.298
- Growing up as a grown up as a kid--

00:08:28.298 --> 00:08:29.131
- Al Capone.

00:08:29.131 --> 00:08:31.530
- Growing up as a kid,
I use to dress like that

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:32.363
everyday for school.

00:08:32.363 --> 00:08:33.200
I'm not kidding.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.030
I used to dress like that, in suits.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:37.240
All day, every day.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:38.330
I was with my dad.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:41.179
We was going to church.

00:08:41.179 --> 00:08:43.250
